<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Serzh Sargsyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Serzh Sargsyan is an Armenian politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh">Nagorno-Karabakh</a> who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> from 2008 to 2018. His election was followed by deadly protests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yerevan">Yerevan</a> in March 2008. In 2018, under a new constitution, he became prime minister, but mass peaceful protests, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velvet-revolution">Velvet Revolution</a>, forced him to resign within days and brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikol-pashinyan">Nikol Pashinyan</a> to power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/serzh-sargsyan.jpg" alt="Serzh Sargsyan" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Пресс-служба Президента Армении · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Serzh_Sargsyan_official_portrait_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
